diff --git a/Docs/PATHFINDING_TRANSPORT_AND_SIEGE.md b/Docs/PATHFINDING_TRANSPORT_AND_SIEGE.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a3ef2ac
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Docs/PATHFINDING_TRANSPORT_AND_SIEGE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,72 @@
+# Pathfinding, transport, siege and settler corrections
+
+These changes apply to GitLab `main` after merge request !34 (tree `e3cbb9a8`). They
+were built with Visual C++ Toolkit 2003 and the Platform SDK for Windows Server 2003
+SP1 and checked with a clang whole-DLL diagnostic pass. Save format, XML and Python
+are unchanged.
+
+## Path searches stay reusable
+
+The engine's A* continues its previous search when a query passes `bReuse` and the
+start plot and flags match. AI loops rely on that: `AI_pickTargetCity` scores every
+enemy city with one incremental search. Two problems undid it.
+
+- **Other groups' queries ran on the same finder.** `AI_cityTargetUnitsByPath`,
+  `AI_unitTargetMissionAIs` (with a path limit), `AI_isPlotThreatened`, the
+  synchronized-landing check in `AI_assaultSeaReinforce` and the ship search in
+  `AI_loadForCoastalAttack` all queried another group's route between the planning
+  group's own queries. Each one discarded the planner's search, so the next candidate
+  started from scratch. With 12 visible enemy cities and 5 stacks around them, that
+  is 72 full searches where one incremental search suffices. These queries now use
+  `CvSelectionGroup::generatePathSecondary`, which runs on a second finder created in
+  `CvMap::setup` and released in `CvGlobals::uninit`.
+- **Reuse ignored who the stored search belonged to.** The engine compares only the
+  start plot and flags. Another group, the same group after its members changed or it
+  spent moves without moving (pillage, fortify), or the same group on a later turn
+  could continue a search tree that describes other units, and so get stale turn
+  counts. `AIPathReuse.h` records each finder's owner (group, membership epoch, turn
+  and the group's least moves left) and passes reuse to the engine only when all of
+  these match.
+
+`AI_isPlotThreatened` used to run one fresh search per enemy unit, so a 20-unit stack
+cost 20 identical searches. It now searches each enemy group once per call.
+
+## Mission lookups by target unit
+
+`AI_group` (escort and stack grouping) calls `AI_unitTargetMissionAIs` once per
+candidate group, and each call walked every group of the player. That made one
+`AI_group` call cost candidates x groups. A unit-target index
+(`AIMissionTargetIndex::UnitIndex`) now answers repeated queries in the same epoch.
+The first query of an epoch still walks the groups, so a single query costs what it
+did before. The epoch now also changes when a group's target unit changes. The path
+variant used to compute `MAX_INT + 1` for a group with no path that could not all
+move, which counted that group as arriving soon. A loaded transport could then wait
+in port for a group that could never reach it. Such a group no longer counts.
+
+## Decision corrections
+
+- **Siege positioning (`AI_choke`).** Every reachable candidate replaced the previous
+  one, so the stack went to the last plot in scan order rather than the best defensive
+  or choke plot. The best value now wins, and one reusable search serves all
+  candidates (each candidate used to start a fresh search).
+- **Joining a synchronized landing (`AI_assaultSeaReinforce`).** The check "can all
+  cargo fight at the landing plot" was computed and then ignored. Transports carrying
+  artillery joined landings on unseen cities, and transports joined landings whose
+  visible defenders their cargo could not attack. The check is now applied, with the
+  same rule as `AI_assaultSeaTransport`: an empty city is not rejected for lacking
+  defenders.
+- **Worker target choice (`AI_bestCityBuild`).** When the first choice was taken,
+  the second pass compared a plot's raw value against the best value per turn of
+  travel. A distant plot with a slightly higher raw value displaced a near plot worth
+  far more per turn. Both sides are now per-turn values.
+- **Settler on its site (`AI_settleMove`).** A settler whose escort died or was split
+  off on arrival walked back to a city, discarding the trip. It now founds when it
+  stands on its accepted site. The danger check still runs first, and the escort rule
+  still applies everywhere else.
+
+## Tests
+
+`Tools/test_path_queries.py`, `Tools/test_group_queries.py` and
+`Tools/test_unit_ai_corrections.py` compile the production functions against host
+adapters. They are mapped in `Tools/regression_manifest.json`; run all programs with
+`python3 Tools/run_regression_suite.py`.
